        "original_id": "24343abc-c7e7-5efc-9383-d135c5857cee",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Projects: The Periodic Table of Videos, Hello Internet\n- People: Brady Haran, Martyn Poliakoff, Peter Licence, Stephen Liddle, Debbie Kays, Neil Barnes, Sam Tang, CGP Grey\n- Organizations: University of Nottingham, BBC News, YouTube\n- Topics: chemical elements, the periodic table, educational videos, podcasts\n\nFacts:\n- Brady John Haran was born on 18 June 1976 and is an Australian-born British independent filmmaker and video journalist.\n- Brady Haran is known for educational videos and documentary films produced for BBC News and for YouTube channels including Periodic Videos and Numberphile.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is a series of videos about chemical elements and the periodic table.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos is published on YouTube and produced by Brady Haran.\n- The Periodic Table of Videos features Martyn Poliakoff, Peter Licence, Stephen Liddle, Debbie Kays, Neil Barnes, Sam Tang, and others at the University of Nottingham.\n- Hello Internet is an audio podcast hosted by CGP Grey and Brady Haran.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
